<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mian Yar Muhammad Kalhoro</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1719">1719</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mian Yar Muhammad Kalhoro was the founder of Kalhora rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh</a>. Head of a family of hereditary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sufism">Sufi</a> leaders with an armed following, he was recognised by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a> around 1701 as governor of parts of northern Sindh, with the title Khuda Yar Khan. He made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khudabad">Khudabad</a> his capital and ruled until his death in 1719, when his son Nur Muhammad succeeded him.</p></div>
